{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1528223-stealing-from-bluebeard\u2019s-bride-rpg\u2026-thoughts-comments-advice","id":1528223,"title":"Stealing from Bluebeard\u2019s Bride RPG\u2026 Thoughts/Comments/Advice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-08T13:30:25-08:00","id":1528223,"title":"Stealing from Bluebeard\u2019s Bride RPG\u2026 Thoughts/Comments/Advice?","content":"I recently found this RPG (published by Magpie Games) &amp; although it uses the PbtA system it\u2019s got a lot of cool/interesting things that I think can work well w/ the victorian gothic horror themes I\u2019ve got going on in my chronicle. There\u2019s 7 books \u2014 including the core book \u2014 and I\u2019ve just been reading through the PDF samples online. It\u2019s already has given me so much inspo &amp; not gonna lie there\u2019s a couple things I want to straight up steal (reworking slightly of course) but I\u2019m not too keen on shilling out a ton of cash to get the books. There\u2019s a PDF bundle on DriveThruRPG for abt $40 but that\u2019s a lot for me atm.<br /> <br /> So, the most important concept in the game is that The Bride roams the castle, enters various rooms \u2014 each room has four mysterious objects, a threat, and two horrors \u2014 experiencing some crazy shit before opening the door to the forbidden room. Here\u2019s an example room, that I want to steal, from one of the books\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>ROOM THREAT:</b> Religion -&gt; Underworld<br /> <br /> The dark wooden doors have two handles shaped like the keys of a piano, which gleam in the light of the hallway. Pressing down on the keys prompts a soft plinking that echoes through the doors as they open.<br /> The room beckons. You enter, and the door closes behind you.<br /> <br /> This giant circular room has a domed ceiling and is filled with finely made musical instruments \u2014pianos, cellos, flutes, violas, drums, guitars, harmonicas, bells. Any instrument you can imagine can be found here, including a strange metal box with a series of knobs and a long antenna protruding from one end. A circle of high backed chairs, each with a singular sapphire blue candle placed on the seat, surrounds the metal box as if silently waiting for the show to begin. Frescoes depicting a parade of musicians adorn the walls and the marbled floor is decorated in a concentric circular pattern of musical notes.<br /> <br /> <b>MYSTERIOUS OBJECTS</b><br /> Patterns of musical notes on floor<br /> Theremin<br /> Fresco of parading musicians<br /> High backed chairs with sapphire candles<br /> <br /> <b>HORRORS OF THE MUSIC ROOM</b><br /> Theremin: When you run your hand over the strange box, it emits a soft wail. The closer your hand wanders to the antenna, the higher the pitch. As the instruments wail grows louder, crying out like a woman in pain, it contorts into the shape of a woman's torso. Her breasts are mutilated, intestines strung up and tied around her neck, and crimson blood pours onto the floor and mats her flaming red hair. The musical notes laid into the marble floor take on an eerie glow. The screams intensify and a dark power surges through your veins. Insects fly from the instruments with a cacophony of sound, forming a swirling mass around you \u2014the eye of the storm.<br /> <br /> Fresco of parading musicians: Men, women, and merrymakers are depicted in an endless parade. They play instruments, fly kites, and joyfully run from men dressed as devils in some sort of celebration. Each time you look at a different section of the painting, a bride appears in the scene. She has long flowing red hair and is dressed in a nightgown. Her gown is open and her guts are strung up around her throat like the neck of a cello.<br /> <br /> Now the sample didn\u2019t have any stats for these horrors so I tried to go with what I think would be best with the painting\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>BRIDE IN THE FRESCO</b><br /> <br /> A large mural covers an entire wall of the music room. Everything seems normal at first glance - an expertly painted scene from floor to ceiling that depicts an outdoor wedding full of joy, revelry, food, &amp; friends - the redheaded bride starts out in the middle of the painting. Happy &amp; beaming from ear to ear, dressed in all white, beside her equally happy husband. With everything else going on in the painting it\u2019s easy to glance over her &amp; keep looking around the piece. But when you first see the bride everything changes. Her expression morphs into one of confusion &amp; terror. Her husband\u2019s turns into an evil smile w/ blood-curdling fury in his eyes. He holds a blade behind his back. The bride tries to run but they\u2019re no longer outside in the open air. Instead they are in the very room in which you stand. The guests are not happy nor are they friends of the bride. Almost snarling &amp; clearly blood-thirsty they gleefully obey their master\u2019s orders to keep the woman still - by any means necessary. The lackeys are commanded to play music to drown out her screams. When the horrific scene ends the woman has been turned into a human cello (or bass) &amp; her blood coats everything in the room. Her cries &amp; screams haunt anyone who stays in the room long enough to see her murder.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> torment those helping ex-husband, drive new wife insane, avenge murder by killing ex-husband (long term)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 5<br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 3, Wits 2, Resolve 7<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dex 3, Stamina 7<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 1<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Persistent<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Wrathful<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Striking Looks at 2 &amp; Sympathetic<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Madness &amp; Terror, Hypnotic Gaze &amp; Influence at 2 dots<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 13<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4 (just bc i imagine her to be short &amp; fairly skinny)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <br /> Anybody familiar with this RPG wanna take a look at those stats? As always thoughts/comments/advice is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","user":"trynmybest","date":". 01-12-2024, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T13:54:28-08:00","id":1528225,"title":"","content":"Not familiar, but the whole sounds like excellent inspiration for mortal/Geist/Hunter games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}